1. Introduction
The Student Grade Management System is a console-based Python application that records
student marks, assigns grades automatically, and displays class statistics through a simple
menu-driven interface.
2. Objectives
• Store student names and their marks
• Automatically calculate grades from marks
• Display all students and a class summary (total students and average marks)
3. Tools and Technologies
• Language: Python 3
• Data storage: built-in dictionary (in memory)
• Interface: command line using input() and print()
4. System Design
Student records are held in a dictionary students = {name: marks}. The program is organised
into the following functions:
Function Purpose
add_student() Takes a name and marks (0-100) and stores them
view_students() Lists all students with their marks
calculate_grade(marks) Returns the grade for the given marks
show_statistics() Shows total students and average marks
main() Runs the 5-option menu loop
Grading scale
Marks Grade
80 and above A
60 - 79 B
40 - 59 C
Below 40 F
5. Working
On launch the program shows a menu. The user selects an option from 1 to 5:
• 1 - Add a student and marks
• 2 - View all students
• 3 - Show the grade of a particular student
• 4 - Show class statistics
• 5 - Exit
The menu repeats in a loop until the user chooses Exit. Data is kept in memory only for the
duration of the run.
